{"term":"Gemächt","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"organs","subcategory":"penis","concept":"male_genitals","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"archaic","crude":12,"technical":22,"recognition_pct_current":35,"recognition_pct_peak":52,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Archaic and literary German term for the male genitalia, derived from 'machen' (to make/create) in the sense of the organs of generation; refers to the penis and testicles collectively.","english_term":"privy parts","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Found in legal, theological, and literary texts of the 17th–19th centuries; extremely rare in modern spoken German; not vulgar but now sounds stilted and archaic."}
