{"term":"Bolzen","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"organs","subcategory":"penis","concept":"penis","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":55,"technical":0,"recognition_pct_current":50,"recognition_pct_peak":58,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"German slang for penis, literally 'bolt' or 'pin'; emphasizes rigidity and penetrative function.","english_term":"rod","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The verb 'bolzen' independently carries crude sexual connotations (to screw/shag) in informal German; the noun-as-penis sense is clearly derived from the same mechanical metaphor of driven fasteners."}
