{"term":"Bengel","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"organs","subcategory":"penis","concept":"penis","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"dated_slang","crude":28,"technical":0,"recognition_pct_current":32,"recognition_pct_peak":48,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"German dialectal slang for penis; primary meaning is 'rascal,' 'rogue,' or 'naughty boy'; the phallic sense is secondary and largely archaic.","english_term":"rascal","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The penis meaning may derive from association with mischievous or unruly behavior; overwhelmingly known for its 'naughty boy' primary meaning; penis usage is confined to older or dialectal German and may be largely extinct in spoken language."}
